-- title:
--   Ends and smooth-point stalks of a supersingular chart, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ is fixed. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`A.LiesOverPrime q`), $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa(A) =$ `ResidueField A` whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` (a place is such when it is rational, is an affine geometric place, and the value there of the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`), $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, and `hle` records the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change inside Laurent series of the full modular function field of level $M'$) in $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` (the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of reduction to units modulo $q$).
--
--   The base-field data consist of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, together with the hypotheses that $A \cap k_0$ (formally, the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; the approximation hypothesis `hκ` states that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; `halgc` states that $\kappa(A)$ is algebraically closed; an algebra structure of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa(A)$ is given, [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is assumed to be a domain, and an index $\zeta_{\mathrm{ix}} \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is fixed. Finally $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, and $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ consisting exactly of those elements lying in $A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by a nonzero element $\varpi_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for $F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and asserts the following for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ subject to four hypotheses — that the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $F$; that for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; that $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; and that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal — and subject also to a linear-disjointness hypothesis: for every finite $k_0$-subextension $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every finite family $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in $F$ forces all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   For such $F_0, W_0$, let $B$ be a subring of $F$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` and satisfying the following chart hypotheses: the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$; $B$ is contained in the compositum $L$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of $L$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most one; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and there in $W_0$; $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; and $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\varpi_b$, in that $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$. Two further hypotheses concern the modular structure: the element $j$ of $F$, namely the image under the inclusion `hle` of the Laurent series `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` viewed in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, lies in $B$; and $B$ is stable under every level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. The last chart hypothesis identifies the special fibre: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa(A)$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the automorphisms attached to $C_s$) such that $\#C_s = 2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, $\ker \rho = \varpi_b B$, $\rho$ restricted to $A_b$ is the residue map of $A$ followed by $\kappa(A) \to$ `quotField`, every element of `quotField` is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h \in B$, the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field comes from [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), and $\rho$ is equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma, 1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f \in B$, the value of $\rho$ on the latter equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) of $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   Finally, let $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ be a field with a $\kappa(A)$-algebra structure and $R$ a `RegularProlongation A F FSS` — that is, a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism `R.residue` onto $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, cutting out $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ has a scalar multiple with nonzero reduction — subject to the compatibility that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f \in W_0$.
--
--   Then there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{\mathrm{ss}}$ over $\kappa(A)$, an assignment $Q \mapsto S_Q$ of subrings of $F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q : A_b[T] \to S_Q$ and $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa(A)$, and sets $D_Q$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the following properties.
--
--   First, $\#N = q+1$. Second, $Q \notin N$ if and only if the reduction `R.residue` of every element of $B$ that lies in `R.integers` lies in the valuation subring of $Q$. Third, for every $Q \notin N$: the image in $F$ of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C a)$ is that image; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(Ca))$ is the residue class of $a$ in $\kappa(A)$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(T)) = 0$; $S_Q$ is local with $\ker \chi_Q$ its maximal ideal; $S_Q \subseteq L$ and every element of $L$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_Q$, $h \neq 0$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_Q$ is contained in `R.integers`, and an element of $S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` if and only if it is divisible by $\varphi_Q(C\varpi_b)$ in $S_Q$; for every $f \in S_Q$ the reduction `R.residue` of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue class there is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa(A) \to \kappa(Q)$; the reduction of $\varphi_Q(T)$ has $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ equal to $1$; $B \subseteq S_Q$; $S_Q$ is the localisation of $B$ along $Q$, in that $f \in S_Q$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and the reduction of $h$, whenever $h$ lies in `R.integers`, lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ with nonzero residue class there; and $D_Q$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which are rational, for which every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for which, for every $f \in S_Q$, the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$.
--
--   Fourth, the discs separate the points: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some place $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$. Fifth, for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the order $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the element $j$ described above is $\geq 0$. Sixth, equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(F)$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut` acts on places so that $\tau \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$, and for $Q \notin N$ one has `RegularProlongation.smulDisc` $\tau\,(D_Q) = D_{\tau \cdot Q}$, where `smulDisc` sends a set $D$ to $\{P \mid \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D\}$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case, at a rigid auxiliary level, of the description of the supersingular component of a semistable model of $X_H$ read off an affine chart $B$ whose special fibre is the quotient Drinfeld curve: the $q+1$ ends $N$ of the component are identified as the places of the reduced function field at which some reduction from $B$ has a pole, and at each remaining place $Q$ the stalk is exhibited as the localisation $S_Q$ of $B$, equipped with an étale coordinate $\varphi_Q$ over $A_b$, a residue character $\chi_Q$ and the corresponding residue disc $D_Q$ of rational places of $F$, all compatible with the level automorphisms. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_three_of_dvd) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
